= Feminism

A Marxist party that excludes women is no Marxist party at all. Still, the dominance of men in both leadership and representation alienate women. How will we deal with this?

-@leadership
-@campaign_women
-@message_change
-@nothing

@leadership
title: Push for more women in local and national leadership.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; women_connection += 2; left_opposition_dissent += 6; right_opposition_dissent += 6; marxist_leninist_dissent += 6; conciliator_dissent += 6

We have increased leadership positions for women. Some of them repalced male leaders, leaving some discontent.

@campaign_women
title: Include and acknowledge the voices of women within our media and propaganda
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; women_connection += 1; new_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 2; new_middle_kpd += 2; workers_kpd += 2

We change and create newspapers and posters to adress women specifically. Some of these are even written by women. This attracts leftist women who may be lured to the SPD otherwise.

@message_change
title: Change our rhetoric to appeal to the new women.
subtitle: This may anger our more hardline communists.
on-arrival: women_connection += 1; left_opposition_dissent += 10; marxist_leninist_dissent += 10

We have attempt to target the women of the new middle class, also known as "new women". While effective at expanding our base, many belive to be dilluting our class character.

@nothing

We have decided to postpone this matter for later, hopefully it doesn't backfire...

- @return: Continue...